      "content": "I'll start by reading both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The original file has unused fields (`record`, `recordWithHeader`, `headerMap`), an unused helper method (`validateMap`), and many unused imports — all carried over from a shared test class. I'll write a clean version that removes the dead code and improves variable naming and structure.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiles successfully (`COMPILE_OK`). The refactored version removes all unused fields, imports, and the `validateMap` helper that were dead code in this single-test file, simplifies `setUp` away entirely by using a static constant, and renames `record1` → `record` and moves `headerMap` into the test method for clarity, while keeping the exact same method calls and assertion."
